§ `Part B: entries that say what a word includes or does not include`

-- F47: "includes" is an open list; "does not include" excludes only what it names

GIVEN w IS A `A word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule`
GIVETH AN `An entry in the Schedule`
`entry` w MEANS `the Part 1 entry for` w

-- line 217: "affidavit", in the case of a person for the time being allowed by law to declare instead of swearing, includes declaration
#ASSERT     `the entry names the thing` (`entry` affidavit) "declaration" TRUE
-- the case does not exist: the entry gives nothing, so FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the entry names the thing` (`entry` affidavit) "declaration" FALSE
-- "includes" is open: a thing the entry does not name is not answered
#ASSERT REFUSED `the entry names the thing` (`entry` affidavit) "a sworn statement" TRUE BECAUSE "an entry that says includes does not close the list, so a thing it does not name is not answered"
-- the case is checked before the list, so a thing that is not named, in a case that does not exist, is FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the entry names the thing` (`entry` affidavit) "a sworn statement" FALSE

-- line 233: "oath", in the case of a person for the time being allowed by law to affirm or declare instead of swearing, includes affirmation or declaration
#ASSERT     `the entry names the thing` (`entry` oath) "affirmation or declaration" TRUE
#ASSERT     `the entry names the thing` (`entry` oath) "affirmation" TRUE
#ASSERT     `the entry names the thing` (`entry` oath) "declaration" TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the entry names the thing` (`entry` oath) "affirmation or declaration" FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the entry names the thing` (`entry` oath) "affirmation" FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the entry names the thing` (`entry` oath) "declaration" FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the entry names the thing` (`entry` oath) "a promise" TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the entry names the thing` (`entry` oath) "affirmation or promise" TRUE BECAUSE "an entry that says includes does not close the list, so a thing it does not name is not answered"

-- line 244: "swear", in the case of a person for the time being allowed by law to affirm or declare instead of swearing, includes affirm and declare
