§ `Part B: sections 21(1) and 21(2) with section 4(1)`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Where a contrary intention appears`
`contrary intention` a b c MEANS
    `Where a contrary intention appears` WITH `in this Act` IS a, `in the enactment itself` IS b, `in the Act under which it is made` IS c

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of enactment`
      says IS A `What an enactment says about its own commencement`
      day IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Facts about an enactment`
`an enactment` k says day MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment` WITH `its kind` IS k, `what it says about commencement` IS says, `the day of its passing or making` IS day

-- line 185: Part 1 of the Schedule applies "in an enactment", so there is no commencement condition; section 4(1) still lets a contrary intention displace it
#ASSERT `section 21(1) gives the Part 1 word its meaning in the enactment` land (`contrary intention` FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (`the Part 1 entry for` land)
#ASSERT `section 21(1) gives the Part 1 word its meaning in the enactment` land (`contrary intention` FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST (`the Part 1 entry for` land)
#ASSERT `section 21(1) gives the Part 1 word its meaning in the enactment` land (`contrary intention` TRUE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 21(1) gives the Part 1 word its meaning in the enactment` land (`contrary intention` FALSE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 21(1) gives the Part 1 word its meaning in the enactment` land (`contrary intention` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING

-- line 186: Part 2 applies "in an enactment which comes into operation after the commencement of this Act" (the end of 31 December 2005)
-- a statutory instrument expressed to come into operation on 2 January 2006: after
#ASSERT `section 21(2) gives the Part 2 word its meaning in the enactment` `working day` (`an enactment` `a statutory instrument` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2006 1 2)) (JUST (YMD 2005 12 1))) (`contrary intention` FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (`the Part 2 entry for` `working day`)
-- expressed to come into operation on 1 January 2006: the same moment, not after (F23)
#ASSERT `section 21(2) gives the Part 2 word its meaning in the enactment` `working day` (`an enactment` `a statutory instrument` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2006 1 1)) (JUST (YMD 2005 12 1))) (`contrary intention` FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- an earlier enactment
#ASSERT `section 21(2) gives the Part 2 word its meaning in the enactment` `full age` (`an enactment` `a statutory instrument` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2005 6 1)) (JUST (YMD 2005 5 1))) (`contrary intention` FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a later enactment, contrary intention in the enactment itself
#ASSERT `section 21(2) gives the Part 2 word its meaning in the enactment` `full age` (`an enactment` `a statutory instrument` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2030 1 1)) (JUST (YMD 2029 1 1))) (`contrary intention` FALSE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 21(2) gives the Part 2 word its meaning in the enactment` `full age` (`an enactment` `a statutory instrument` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2030 1 1)) (JUST (YMD 2029 1 1))) (`contrary intention` FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (`the Part 2 entry for` `full age`)
-- an Act that says nothing, passed on 1 January 2006 itself: no moment is named (s 16(1)), so not answered
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 21(2) gives the Part 2 word its meaning in the enactment` `functions` (`an enactment` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` (JUST (YMD 2006 1 1))) (`contrary intention` FALSE FALSE NOTHING) BECAUSE "section 16(1) names no moment within the date of passing, so whether an enactment that came into operation on 1 January 2006 did so after this Act is not answered"
-- an Act that says nothing, passed on 2 January 2006: after
#ASSERT `section 21(2) gives the Part 2 word its meaning in the enactment` `functions` (`an enactment` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` (JUST (YMD 2006 1 2))) (`contrary intention` FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (`the Part 2 entry for` `functions`)
